  "releaseNotes": "The intake side of security events as route handlers: the OpenID Back-Channel Logout endpoint a relying party exposes, and the push delivery endpoint of RFC 8935 that a transmitter posts to. Each validates the token through the Security Events core before handing it on, answers with the status codes the specifications prescribe, and needs no MVC framework in the host. Full details: https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/releases/tag/v3.0",
